A cosmic orchestra in the style of Vincent van Gogh, swirling night sky filled with twelve luminous celestial particles spiraling in dynamic motion, each particle a different vibrant color—gold, teal, crimson, violet—trailing brushstroke energy waves behind them. Four massive force fields visualized as interconnected spiral galaxies in the background, rendered with thick impasto technique and characteristic starry night turbulence. Musical staff lines weave organically through the cosmos like aurora ribbons, with planets and atoms dancing along them as if they were notes. The composition bursts with movement and wonder, deep midnight blues contrasting with brilliant yellows and whites, capturing the harmonious dance of fundamental physics as pure visual poetry.
